        "execSummary":  "The Kinaxis story illustrates a maturing pattern in enterprise AI: purpose-built vertical platforms that embed AI agents directly into operational workflows, rather than general-purpose assistants layered on top of existing systems. The 120% surge in scenario modeling reflects a market reality — geopolitical instability is making continuous AI-assisted planning a competitive necessity, not an optimization project. For enterprise technology leaders, this is a signal to audit which operational domains are still running on periodic human-led planning cycles that could be replaced with AI-driven continuous monitoring. The Microsoft angle here is platform affinity — Kinaxis runs on Azure, reinforcing the cloud platform as the substrate for enterprise AI at scale.",
