        "summary":  "AWS introduces the Adjudicated Query pattern, which combines Amazon Q\u0027s conversational AI interface with a deterministic rules engine to deliver provably complete compliance decisions across tens of thousands of lease documents. The design deliberately separates AI-driven inquiry from rule-based adjudication, ensuring every record is accounted for with a defensible audit trail. This hybrid approach addresses the core limitation of generative AI in regulated contexts: the inability to guarantee completeness and determinism.",
        "execSummary":  "For compliance-heavy enterprise functions — legal, finance, real estate, HR — the Adjudicated Query pattern represents a mature architectural answer to a recurring AI deployment blocker: how do you use generative AI for scale without sacrificing auditability? By routing all pass/fail decisions through a deterministic rules engine and using AI only for natural-language inquiry and orchestration, the pattern produces outputs defensible in regulatory or legal proceedings. Enterprise leaders evaluating AI for compliance workflows should view this as a reference architecture worth adopting broadly, not just for leases. The critical dependency is maintaining the rules engine alongside AI updates — governance of the rules layer becomes the new compliance obligation.",
