        "summary":  "A sponsored analysis argues that enterprise AI has moved from experimentation into full operational deployment, with global AI investment projected to reach $2.5 trillion in 2026 — a 44% year-over-year increase. The report identifies siloed intelligence, rigid technology architectures, and unresolved AI sovereignty questions as the primary barriers to enterprise-wide value capture. The recommended response involves restructuring data infrastructure, adopting composable architectures, and resolving cross-border data governance before scaling autonomous AI.",
        "execSummary":  "This report provides a useful executive-level framework for diagnosing why many enterprises see AI pilots succeed but enterprise-wide transformation stall: the bottleneck is architectural fragmentation, not model capability. The shift to autonomous AI operating models requires data infrastructure investment, composable systems replacing monolithic platforms, and resolved AI sovereignty policies — prerequisites most large organizations have not yet completed. For enterprise and customer-support leaders, the actionable implication is to audit whether your AI deployment can share learnings across business units or whether intelligence accumulates in departmental silos. The sponsored nature of the report means its solution framing leans toward Uniphore\u0027s product positioning; treat the diagnostic framework as valuable, vendor recommendations as starting points.",
