        "source":  "CIO.com",
        "url":  "https://www.cio.com/article/4226418/ai-agents-a-lot-of-effort-but-still-little-return.html",
        "date":  "2026-10-02",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Despite 89% of companies regularly using AI, only 37% report any positive EBIT impact, with agent-based workflows consuming 5-30x more compute than standard chatbot queries. The resource intensity caused 93% of surveyed organizations to exceed their AI budgets. Improved orchestration frameworks from Anthropic, OpenAI, and LangGraph are maturing but returns remain elusive.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise AI agents are delivering underwhelming ROI at significant cost: only 37% of companies see positive EBIT impact, and agent workflows burn 5-30 times more compute than chatbots, blowing budgets at 93% of organizations surveyed. The implication for enterprise leaders is that agentic AI is not yet a cost-effective at-scale play — it is a high-investment, early-stage bet. Before expanding agent deployments, CIOs should demand clear ROI metrics and compute cost guardrails. The maturing of orchestration tools from Anthropic and OpenAI suggests the economics will improve, but leaders who commit large budgets today are doing so ahead of proven returns.",
