        "summary":  "Microsoft and Google are backing Apache Ossie, an open specification using JSON and YAML to exchange semantic models across data, analytics, and AI platforms. Over 60 companies including Databricks, Nvidia, Salesforce, Snowflake, and Oracle support the initiative. Microsoft is building a two-way converter between Power BI and Ossie to enable portability of business logic across platforms.",
        "execSummary":  "Apache Ossie represents a significant industry push to reduce vendor lock-in across enterprise data and AI platforms, with backing from Microsoft, Google, and 60+ major vendors. For enterprise leaders, this matters because it could eventually allow semantic models — the business logic embedded in analytics and AI tools — to move freely between platforms like Snowflake, Databricks, and Tableau. Analysts caution that broad vendor participation does not guarantee proprietary lock-in disappears in practice. CIOs evaluating platform consolidation or multi-cloud AI strategies should track Ossie adoption as a signal of which vendors are genuinely committed to interoperability versus using the standard as a marketing signal.",
